1
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:20,720
Anyone who's broke, come to me.

2
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:25,400
I'm broke too, but don't worry.

3
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:29,280
Look at that blue sky.

4
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:32,500
White clouds.

5
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:39,140
It'll all work out somehow, eventually.

6
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,440
You understand, right?

7
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:44,420
I know, I know.

8
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:48,300
Once you get it,
just keep quiet and follow me.

9
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,640
The World's Number One Police Showdown.

10
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,520
I'm terribly sorry.

11
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:14,940
Hey, hey, what's this all of a sudden?

12
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:19,980
Yes, well, I suppose our Ryotsu
has gone and done something again.

13
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:22,440
I really am terribly sorry.

14
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:25,760
I've been telling him over and over,
day in and day out.

15
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:30,640
We didn't call you here
because Ryotsu-kun did something.

16
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:35,360
It does have to do with Ryotsu-kun, though.

17
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:38,220
How so?

18
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:44,320
The truth is, Interpol is holding a contest to
determine the world's number one police officer.

19
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:49,860
Interpol presents

20
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:53,460
World Policeman Championship

21
00:01:53,460 --> 00:02:00,220
from the 179 countries
belonging to Interpol,

22
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:02,540
gathering the finest police officers

23
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:05,540
to determine the world's
number one police officer.

24
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:09,100
So it's like an Olympics
for police officers?

25
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:09,700
That's right.

26
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,780
That sounds interesting.

27
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:13,720
What a wonderful endeavor.

28
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:16,760
Interpol headquarters has
made a request to our country

29
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:21,340
They've nominated Inspector Kitano of the
Special Crimes Division as a contestant.

30
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:23,660
Inspector Kitano?

31
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:25,740
The Kaipan-deka?

32
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:28,040
His attire is a bit questionable,
Translation>
but

33
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:32,180
he's maintained a 100% arrest
rate for the past ten years,

34
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:34,260
so it's only natural.

35
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:35,160
I see.

36
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:38,600
Besides the Kaipan-deka,
Translation>
Interpol

37
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:42,460
has asked us to recommend
two police officers from Japan.

38
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:45,180
So we used a computer

39
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:48,200
to search for officers
with a 100% arrest rate,

40
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:51,000
and we were able to narrow it down to two.

41
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,220
And both of them are officers
from Katsushika Station!

42
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:57,500
Is that so?

43
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:59,420
Chief, what an honor.

44
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,880
So who are the two?

45
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:04,780
One is Officer Nakagawa Keiichi.

46
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:09,180
Well done, Ohara! Isn't he your subordinate?

47
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:10,880
I'm honored.

48
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:12,940
And the other one is...

49
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:16,680
Ryotsu? You're saying Ryotsu?

50
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:19,400
That must be some kind of mistake.

51
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:21,860
No, Senior Officer Ryotsu is

52
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:24,360
just like Officer Nakagawa, the Kaipan Deka,

53
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:26,620
he had a 100% arrest rate.

54
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:27,960
Well, I suppose you could call them cases,

55
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:30,040
but they were things like dine-and-dashers,
petty thieves,

56
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,360
and pickpockets. Petty offenses, really.

57
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:33,320
So, that being the case,

58
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:36,300
as far as we're concerned, we intend to
send Officer Nakagawa and Officer Ryotsu

59
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:38,400
to the competition.

60
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:40,200
Please wait, Commissioner.

61
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,900
Nakagawa, that's one thing,

62
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,520
but if we send Ryotsu to compete,

63
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:50,980
please, leave this matter to us.
We absolutely won't let anything bad happen.

64
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:52,080
Please.

65
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:06,300
I never imagined Ryotsu would be chosen as Japan's
representative for the World's No.1 Police Officer Championship.

66
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:12,900
Yeah, I had no idea that guy who does nothing
but write incident reports had a 100% arrest rate.

67
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:17,300
The problem is how to
keep Ryotsu from competing.

68
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:19,880
Ohara, do you have any good ideas?

69
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:21,220
Well, let me think.

70
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,240
How about this?

71
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:27,500
Calling it a reward
for his 100% arrest rate,

72
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:31,580
if we give him about a week
off during the tournament...

73
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:32,700
I see.

74
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:36,920
That guy has already used up all
his paid vacation for this year.

75
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:39,060
He'll jump at it for sure.

76
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:41,060
Mm-hmm, let's go with that.

77
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:43,120
Throw in a hot spring trip too.

78
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,320
That's good.

79
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:46,140
He's really going to take the bait

80
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:48,420
Ahahahahahaha!

81
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:49,700
Ahahahaha!

82
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:58,280
I heard that, I heard that,
you sneaky old tanuki geezers!

83
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,980
The World No.1 Police Officer Championship

84
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:04,480
This sounds like fun.

85
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:07,980
The Station Chief and the Chief are trying to keep me from competing,
aren't they?

86
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:09,140
Just you watch.

87
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:13,000
Nakagawa, I heard about it.

88
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:17,780
They say you've been picked to represent Japan
in the World No.1 Police Officer Championship.

89
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:18,980
Yeah, well...

90
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:21,000
That's amazing, Kei-chan!

91
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,980
It's just that my arrest rate
happened to be good last year.

92
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:28,120
Nakagawa, please do your best and win it!

93
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:33,300
But the competition is all outstanding police officers from around the world,
you know.

94
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:36,840
So what does the winner actually get?

95
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:43,100
If it's such a big competition, there must
be a hefty cash prize or something, right?

96
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:46,240
Yes, the winner's prize money
is apparently 100 million yen.

97
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:49,400
What, 100 million yen?

98
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:56,800
Plus a free lifetime pass to use first
class on airlines all over the world,

99
00:05:57,380 --> 00:06:02,740
and a gold card for free meals at every three-star restaurant in the world,
apparently.

100
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:03,120
Well,

101
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:05,420
that's amazing!

102
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:10,780
Well, that's none of your business, Ryo-chan.
You're the police officer furthest from being a representative.

103
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:14,920
Shut up! Is there no one else
to represent Japan besides you?

104
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:20,180
Because Kaipan-deka has had a 100%
arrest rate for ten straight years,

105
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:23,100
he's apparently competing
as a seeded player.

106
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,480
Kaipan-deka

107
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:29,080
If you ask me,
he's the disgrace of the Japanese police.

108
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:30,060
Morning.

109
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:31,900
Good morning.

110
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:35,460
Chief, we heard about Nakagawa-kun!

111
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:36,360
That's amazing.

112
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:39,340
Nakagawa, I wish you the best of luck!

113
00:06:39,340 --> 00:06:40,000
Thank you very much.

114
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:42,480
And Ryotsu,

115
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:44,820
I've got some good news for you too.

116
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:52,220
I didn't notice at all,
but apparently your arrest rate is 100% too.

117
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:54,380
Ryo-chan's?

118
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,600
Though it's mostly arrests for
dine-and-dashers and petty thieves.

119
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:59,040
That's surprising.

120
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:05,160
The chief was overjoyed too,
and he's going to give you a special award.

121
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:08,040
That groveling chief?

122
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:10,360
What, aren't you happy?

123
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:14,160
No, no! What are they giving me?

124
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:16,260
Alright,
don't be too surprised when you hear it.

125
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:20,100
A week's leave and a free hot spring pass.

126
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:23,040
Yay, I'm so happy!

127
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,700
Surprised

128
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:28,460
Wait a moment, Chief.

129
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:31,840
If your arrest rate is also 100%, senpai,

130
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:34,220
then you're also a world No.
1 police officer.

131
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:37,080
Don't say unnecessary things.

132
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:40,080
What's wrong, Chief?

133
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,800
It's nothing.

134
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:45,120
Anyway, the station chief wants
to give you a special award,

135
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,980
so he said to come to the station.

136
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:49,240
Come on, go on, get going!

137
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:52,820
Well then, I'm off for a bit!

138
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:55,520
Don't be rude to the chief.

139
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:58,140
Make sure you thank him properly.

140
00:07:58,840 --> 00:07:59,680
Yeah, yeah.

141
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,720
Here we go.

142
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:05,940
Therefore,

143
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:09,500
I expect Nakagawa Ryo to do his very best,

144
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:14,260
and show the world just how
capable Japan's police officers are.

145
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:17,640
I sincerely wish you both the best of luck.

146
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:19,700
Thank you very much.

147
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:28,600
Ohara, Ryotsu did actually go on his trip,
didn't he?

148
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:31,700
Yes. Yesterday we went
all the way to the station

149
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:35,240
and even gave him an ekiben for the road,
so there's nothing to worry about.

150
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:37,380
Next,

151
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:38,500
Wait a minute!

152
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,720
Ryotsu!

153
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:43,500
Senpai!

154
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,700
Commissioner-General,

155
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:53,060
Ryotsu...

156
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:54,340
what do you think you're doing?

157
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:57,220
I'd like to ask the
Commissioner-General something.

158
00:08:57,220 --> 00:08:58,520
What is it?

159
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:01,440
That's disrespectful to
the Commissioner-General!

160
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:04,280
Besides,
weren't you supposed to be on a trip?

161
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:06,480
That was a token of appreciation,

162
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,740
so I gratefully accepted it

163
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:11,460
and I cashed it in.

164
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:13,000
W-what?!

165
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:14,680
Commissioner-General, right?

166
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:17,220
Aside from the seeded overseas players,

167
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:19,020
as for the other Japanese representative,

168
00:09:19,020 --> 00:09:21,600
the one with the best arrest rate last year,

169
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,220
I heard was chosen, but

170
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:24,320
is that true?

171
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:26,320
Yes, that's right.

172
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:27,960
Members of the press,

173
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:30,960
actually, I, Kankichi Ryotsu,

174
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:32,780
had last year's arrest rate

175
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,820
of 100%.

176
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:37,800
Despite that,

177
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:39,280
for some reason, I

178
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:41,120
wasn't chosen for the team.

179
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:45,460
What on earth is going on here?

180
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:51,600
Hold on, Officer Ryotsu.

181
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:54,260
The selection criteria
for Japan's representative

182
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,240
aren't based on arrest rate alone.

183
00:09:56,820 --> 00:10:00,000
You also have to excel at
shooting and martial arts.

184
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:00,700
Stop!

185
00:10:01,220 --> 00:10:04,440
Nakagawa, at last year's Metropolitan
Police shooting competition,

186
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:06,560
what place did I get again?

187
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:10,860
Yes, if I recall, you took second place,
behind champion Volvo Saigo.

188
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:14,600
And how did I do at the National
Police Judo Championship?

189
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:18,740
You lost on points to Sanedera-san
after extra time and took runner-up.

190
00:10:18,740 --> 00:10:21,420
By the way, at the kendo tournament,

191
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:22,600
you won first place.

192
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:25,820
Yes, yes, thank you, Nakagawa.

193
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:29,200
Despite all that,
it's unthinkable that I wasn't chosen.

194
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:31,820
Why is that, Commissioner-General?

195
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:35,760
Because there was a report
that you committed a violation.

196
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:38,140
I haven't committed any violations.

197
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:41,400
But I clearly heard it from Tonda-kun,

198
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:44,060
Chief, what is going on?

199
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:45,360
Well, that is...

200
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:47,300
Be quiet!

201
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:51,320
A useless cop who writes over
100 self-criticism reports a year

202
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:54,940
can't be allowed to compete in the championship,
obviously!

203
00:10:54,940 --> 00:11:00,120
Then I'll ask the executives
who chose the representatives.

204
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:05,360
Was there a directive from Interpol to include the
number of self-criticism reports in the selection criteria

205
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:11,980
Is that so? There was no such directive,
yet I wasn't selected.

206
00:11:11,980 --> 00:11:21,780
Depending on how this goes, I might file a protest with Interpol.
Understood? It was our mistake.

207
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:24,160
We've decided to add you
as an additional entry.

208
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:26,260
Hm.

209
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:30,340
Heh. Thank you very much!

210
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:34,460
This is the worst-case scenario.

211
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:39,300
Hahaha! Ryotsu, you're entering too?

212
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:45,600
This is getting interesting. Let's both
aim for the championship and do our best!

213
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:46,280
Great.

214
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:46,860
That's right.

215
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:53,560
That Kaipan guy

216
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:57,060
I'm definitely going
to win the championship!

217
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:04,460
Why do I have to go all the way to France?

218
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:08,900
Shut up! I know what you're gonna say next,

219
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:11,480
even though I had a date
with Nana-chan tomorrow.

220
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:12,880
Right?

221
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:15,420
I'm sick of hearing it every single time.

222
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:19,660
You knew that and still dragged me here?

223
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:21,100
That's harsh.

224
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:22,520
Senpai.

225
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:25,940
Under the rules of the World
Number One Police Championship,

226
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:31,640
participants are allowed up to
two assistants as support, right?

227
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:34,920
I asked Volvo-san and Sakonji-san,

228
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:38,180
but who's the other one
besides Honda-san, Senpai?

229
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,340
I've got it all set up.

230
00:12:40,340 --> 00:12:42,640
I've got an ace up my sleeve, you know.

231
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:44,440
An ace up my sleeve.

232
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:48,840
You'll find out when we get there.

233
00:13:04,140 --> 00:13:07,000
As police officers, we pledge

234
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,620
to compete with honor and fair play.

235
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:17,560
Senpai, what is that coffin?

236
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:19,100
This?

237
00:13:19,860 --> 00:13:23,860
I didn't have a duffel bag,
so I just brought this instead.

238
00:13:23,860 --> 00:13:26,500
Even so, a coffin? Isn't that a bit much?

239
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:30,300
It's a free country. What I bring is my business,
so don't worry about it.

240
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:34,820
Before we head to Monaco,
where the first event is being held,

241
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:37,500
let me introduce the seeded
competitors for this tournament.

242
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:42,420
First, representing Italy, Ferrari Deka.

243
00:13:42,420 --> 00:13:49,020
Ferrari Deka Nakagawa,
looks like they took your little box.

244
00:13:49,420 --> 00:13:55,120
That's why, for the first event's race, I
brought a special patrol car, a tuned-up Porsche.

245
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:59,060
Next, representing China, Ramen Deka.

246
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:06,660
Ramen Man? Are you kidding me?

247
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:18,180
Kenya's representative: Savanna Deka,
lover of nature

248
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:24,220
UK representative: Scotch Deka

249
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:28,380
USA representative: Manhattan Deka

250
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:31,560
Russia's representative: Cossack Deka

251
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:35,880
What a gathering of freaks, huh

252
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:40,480
And finally,
Japan's representative: Kaipan Deka

253
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:44,580
Hey, hey, there's nobody here!

254
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:48,660
What's that bastard doing,
late for the opening ceremony?

255
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:52,880
It's not just a bulge in my crotch,
it's style

256
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,940
When a serious case breaks out

257
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:57,620
One kaihan stamp solves everything

258
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:03,940
One of the Sanba Glass from Japan's Metropolitan
Police Special Investigation Division

259
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:07,220
With a kaihan, I'm reborn!

260
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,200
Manny Shiro, is that you?

261
00:15:18,340 --> 00:15:21,240
The first event of the World
Number One Isolation Championship

262
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:23,700
uses the course of the F1 Monaco Grand Prix,

263
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:27,380
a race testing driving skill using
patrol cars and white-and-black barriers.

264
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:31,300
Today's race commentary

265
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:33,840
comes from Katsushika Police Station of
the Japan Metropolitan Police Department.

266
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:37,960
We have Chief Honda and
Senior Officer Ohara with us.

267
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:39,660
Nice to meet you.

268
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:41,280
Pleased to be here.

269
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:46,540
Starting from pole position is Italy's Ferrari Deka,
the favorite in this event.

270
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:53,320
And in second place is Japan's Nakagawa,
driving a custom-built Porsche patrol car.

271
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:58,340
When chasing a suspect,
all sorts of unexpected obstacles await.

272
00:15:58,340 --> 00:16:04,080
This race tests how quickly you can reach the goal
while avoiding the various obstacles set up on the course,

273
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:09,400
testing an officer's split-second judgment
and precise driving skill in this obstacle race.

274
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:13,360
Savanna, a lover of nature,
has deliberately entered with an ostrich.

275
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:18,500
And Ryotsu is entering in a
rather old-fashioned patrol car.

276
00:16:18,500 --> 00:16:23,080
Ryotsu is clearly completely unprepared,
I'd say.

277
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:29,020
With something that old, he has no chance of winning.
And that's not even a patrol car, it's a taxi!

278
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:33,700
The top 16 finishers advance to the next event,
a survival race.

279
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:41,560
And 32 cars are now starting all at once!

280
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,860
Ferrari is getting off to a strong start,
and Nakagawa...

281
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:45,340
Dashing off in a daze.

282
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:47,140
Taoru is way out in front!

283
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:50,260
Oh my, what could be the matter?

284
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:52,440
Isn't that one of the top
contenders to win, Kaipan?

285
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,920
One after another, they're being passed.

286
00:17:01,220 --> 00:17:02,880
Why isn't he picking up speed?

287
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:08,980
First, let's see everyone's skills.

288
00:17:18,820 --> 00:17:19,720
There it is!

289
00:17:25,900 --> 00:17:27,400
Aaaah!

290
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:35,860
Watchō! A sudden accident!

291
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:39,700
Ferrari Deka,
the number one favorite in this event!

292
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:40,840
It's a crash!

293
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:57,420
At the first obstacle, lots of patrol
cars are spinning out and crashing!

294
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,700
Spreading oil across the course...

295
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:03,500
A criminal trying to get away would stoop to that,
wouldn't they?

296
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:07,080
Well, I suppose it's not impossible.

297
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:08,600
That was close.

298
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:15,840
Wow, amazing!

299
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:22,500
I knew I'd need it,
so the modifications are perfect!

300
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:23,880
Oops, slipped up there.

301
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:24,200
See?

302
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:29,040
Senpai!

303
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:30,640
Nakagawa! See you later!

304
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:36,140
Hehehe! Bye, everyone!

305
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:40,120
This is what they call benefiting
from another's misfortune.

306
00:18:40,120 --> 00:18:44,060
As expected of Senpai! To have done
such modifications in such a short time!

307
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:57,400
Now, the racers who
cleared the first obstacle,

308
00:18:57,880 --> 00:18:59,240
are gradually picking up speed.

309
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:01,960
From here, the course is an uphill climb.

310
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:05,600
Whoa!

311
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:08,500
A giant iron ball suddenly appears!

312
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:16,180
Whoa, they've all fled!

313
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:20,860
Police officers must be able to dodge
the criminal's iron ball attack, right?

314
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:24,500
Do fleeing criminals use iron balls?

315
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:47,340
!

316
00:19:47,340 --> 00:19:47,720
Yes!

317
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:51,260
How about that?

318
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:56,180
Ryotsu's taxi?
I didn't expect him to modify it that far.

319
00:19:56,180 --> 00:19:57,860
Then here's mine.

320
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:02,388
I see,

321
00:20:02,438 --> 00:20:06,180
so that's one way to do it.

322
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:12,760
Kaipan Deka clears the iron
ball with skillful driving!

323
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:16,900
Nakagawa's racer is clearing
the Manhattan Deka the same way.

324
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:20,480
Otsuka's racers are clearing it
one after another in the same way.

325
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:21,520
I see.

326
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:24,540
When the criminal
attacks with the iron ball,

327
00:20:24,540 --> 00:20:26,860
it seems you're supposed
to dodge it this way.

328
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:32,080
And now Savanna Deka takes the
lead as it comes out of the tunnel!

329
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:41,120
We made it through the hairpin.

330
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:43,720
Alright, only the final corner is left.

331
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:49,860
Nakagawa, don't rush!
There's bound to be another obstacle.

332
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:52,620
You're young, Nakagawa.

333
00:20:57,820 --> 00:21:01,700
The last obstacle is a rippling road!

334
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:04,460
That's absolutely impossible.

335
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,480
How are we supposed to
drive on a course like this?

336
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:14,620
W-wow, that's amazing!

337
00:21:15,220 --> 00:21:18,440
Hey, look! Just as I thought!

338
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:21,060
Watch this! Just press the button!

339
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:24,780
Nakagawa, after you!

340
00:21:26,220 --> 00:21:27,400
How about that? Did you see it?

341
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:30,960
Looks like we have no choice
but to force our way through here.

342
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:31,620
Alright!

343
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:37,500
Aaaaaaah!

344
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,540
Aaaaaaah!

345
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:45,420
Amazing evasion! Alright, let's go!

346
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:46,880
Aaaaaaah!

347
00:21:50,780 --> 00:21:52,220
Eeeeeeeh?!

348
00:21:53,880 --> 00:22:06,420
Aaaaaaah! Aaaaaaah!

349
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:13,880
Japan's representative, Kaipan Deka.

350
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:15,560
has just crossed the
finish line in first place.

351
00:22:17,940 --> 00:22:20,180
In second place is Kenya's representative,
Savanna Deka.

352
00:22:20,660 --> 00:22:23,760
Next, Japan's representatives,
Ryotsu and Nakagawa,

353
00:22:23,760 --> 00:22:25,460
are crossing the finish
line one after another.

354
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:30,900
As expected,
most of the seeded racers have finished,

355
00:22:30,900 --> 00:22:31,660
but

356
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:34,560
America's representative, Manhattan Deka,

357
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:37,200
is stalled in front of the course.

358
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:55,740
What a pushy bastard!

359
00:22:56,100 --> 00:22:59,360
Is that the pride of a seeded racer,
Manhattan Deka?

360
00:22:59,360 --> 00:23:01,620
He's crossed the finish line
with some pretty wild moves.

361
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:05,020
In the end,
only 12 racers have reached the finish.

362
00:23:05,020 --> 00:23:08,780
That really shows how
brutal this race has been.

363
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:12,320
The real contest starts now.

364
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:15,220
I'm definitely taking that 100 million yen!

